# Keywords

Print vocabulary lives in [`docs/KEYWORDS.md`](docs/KEYWORDS.md). The **Rules**
tab shows its player sections (HTML comments are agent-only).

When authoring cards, new mechanics, hooks, tokens, keywords, or other rules
print:

1. Read `docs/KEYWORDS.md` first.
2. Prefer an existing operator + argument over a new verb — `[Mark N Toxin]`,
   `[Mark N Toxin on attacks]`, `[Forge N]` on their die. Do **not** mint
   Dose / Envenom / Brand / Contaminate for a slightly different window.
3. A new **token** (creature counter, Shield, face marker) gets a rulebook
   paragraph and joins **X** on `[Mark]` / `[Strip]`. It does not get its own
   keyword. Attribute exclusives still gate the **argument**, not the verb.
4. Add a **physics** keyword (`[Empower]`, `[Pierce]`, `[Prevent]`) only when
   the operation is not placing or removing a token.
5. Timing prefixes stay prefixes: `On roll: [Mark 1 Toxin].` Never “Whenever…”.
6. Same change: update `docs/KEYWORDS.md`. If play itself changed, also
   `docs/RULEBOOK.md`. Map print to existing `EffectDefinition` members; do
   not add a generic `mark-token` AST just to match the glossary.

Do not mass-rewrite existing `rulesText` unless asked. **New and edited**
print uses the glossary.
